.\" -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-
.TH SEGLCD 1 "2026-11-20" "seglcd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
seglcd \- test and analysis tool for the Thermaltake segment LCD (LB360-S ARGB Sync)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seglcd
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B seglcd
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seglcd
talks to the segment LCD on the pump block of the Thermaltake LB360-S ARGB Sync
(USB 5131:200e) and the LA series (5131:2007) via HID (hidraw/hidapi).
The display only shows values while it receives an update packet at least every
400\(en500 ms, so all sending commands repeat their packet periodically (keep-alive)
until
.B \-\-duration
elapses or Ctrl+C is pressed.
.PP
For permanent operation use the service
.BR seglcdd (1);
pause it (D-Bus property
.BR Enabled )
before running sending commands, otherwise both programs send alternately.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list \fR[\fB\-\-all\fR]
Show the segment LCDs found (or all HID devices) with path, IDs, usage page,
strings, whether the device can be opened, and the report descriptor.
.TP
.B send \fR[\fIvalues\fR]
Send fixed values:
.BR \-\-cpu\-temp ", " \-\-cpu\-usage ", " \-\-cpu\-power ", " \-\-cpu\-clock ", " \-\-cpu\-voltage ,
.BR \-\-gpu\-temp ", " \-\-gpu\-usage ", " \-\-gpu\-power ", " \-\-gpu\-clock ,
.BR \-\-fan ", " \-\-pump ", " \-\-ram ", " \-\-time
.RI ( ISO\~8601 ),
.BR \-\-fahrenheit ", " \-\-off\-at\-end .
Missing values are sent as 0.
.TP
.B live
Send live sensor values. Sources:
.BR \-\-cpu\-temp\-sensor ", " \-\-cpu\-power\-sensor ", " \-\-cpu\-voltage\-sensor ,
.BR \-\-gpu\-temp\-sensor ", " \-\-gpu\-usage\-sensor ", " \-\-gpu\-power\-sensor ", " \-\-gpu\-clock\-sensor ,
.BR \-\-fan\-sensor ", " \-\-pump\-sensor
(see
.B SENSOR SPECS
below),
.B \-\-cpu\-clock\-mode
.RB ( Avg | Max | Min | First ),
.B \-\-sample\-interval
.I ms
(default 1000),
.B \-\-show
(print the values),
.BR \-\-fahrenheit .
Sends the off packet when finished and reconnects after the device was unplugged.
.TP
.B probe
Set one byte at a time to
.B \-\-value
(default 88) while all others stay 0, to find out which field the display shows.
.B \-\-values
.I list
(e.g. 0,1,50,99,128,255) cycles through a value sequence per byte instead, each value for
.B \-\-value\-seconds
(1); with
.B \-\-auto
once per byte, otherwise until Enter is pressed.
.B \-\-offsets
.I list
(e.g. 3,13,36\-63; default 3\(en63),
.B \-\-auto
.I seconds
(advance automatically),
.B \-\-no\-header
(leave bytes 1/2 free). Interactive keys: Enter next, b back, a number changes the value,
.BI o offset
jumps, q quits.
.TP
.B sweep \fIoffset\fR
Count one byte from
.B \-\-from
to
.B \-\-to
(100) in steps of
.B \-\-step
(1) every
.B \-\-step\-ms
(500);
.B \-\-set
.I offset=value,...
sets further fixed bytes.
.TP
.B raw \fIhex\fR...
Send up to 64 bytes (without report ID, rest filled with 00) periodically, or once with
.BR \-\-once .
.TP
.B off
Send the off packet (00\~0F\~00\~...).
.TP
.B hold
Send for
.B \-\-send
seconds (5) with
.BR \-\-cpu\-temp / \-\-gpu\-temp
(42/57), then stop but keep the device open for
.B \-\-hold
seconds (10). Used to measure the display timeout.
.TP
.B listen
Print input reports;
.B \-\-keep\-alive
sends zero packets in parallel.
.TP
.B sensors
List all sensor sources (hwmon, RAPL, NVIDIA NVML, DRM, cpufreq, meminfo) with the spec to use and the current value.
.TP
.B decode \fR[\fIfile\fR|\fB\-\fR]
Decode hex packets, one per line, optionally preceded by a time and a tab
(output of tools/extract\-packets.sh).
.B \-\-diff
shows only changed bytes,
.B \-\-strip\-report\-id
removes a leading 00 from 65-byte lines.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " path"
Use this device, e.g. /dev/hidraw5 (default: first known segment LCD).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Send nothing, print the (first) packet as hex.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print every packet sent with a time stamp.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " seconds"
Stop after this time (default: until Ctrl+C).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " ms"
Send interval (default 250). Values above 400 cause a warning: the display turns off after about 400\(en500 ms without a packet.
.SH SENSOR SPECS
.TP
.I chip:label
hwmon sensor, e.g. k10temp:Tctl, it8686_31050607:fan5 (stable, preferred).
.TP
.I hwmonN/name
hwmon path, e.g. hwmon5/fan1 (the number may change on reboot).
.TP
.I a+b
Sum, e.g. zenpower:SVI2_P_Core+zenpower:SVI2_P_SoC.
.TP
.BR rapl [ :\fIdomain\fR ]
Power from a RAPL counter: package (default), core, uncore, dram, psys. Root only unless
udev/72\-rapl\-energy\-read.rules is installed.
.TP
.BR nvml [ \fIN\fR ] :\fImetric\fR
NVIDIA GPU N: temperature, power, clock, memclock, usage, fan (%).
.TP
.BR drm [ \fIN\fR ] :\fImetric\fR
DRM card N: busy (%), freq (MHz, Intel).
.SH NOTES
The LB360-S shows only the CPU and GPU temperature, as integers in \(deC, capped at 99.
Do not use
.B \-\-fahrenheit
with it: the symbol stays \(deC and values of 100 and more are shown with two digits (122 \(-> 22).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Display language (e.g. de_DE.UTF-8). LC_ALL and LANGUAGE are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 nothing found or invalid input, 2 device not found or not accessible.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/70\-thermaltake\-segment\-lcd.rules
Gives the logged-in user access to the device.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
seglcd list
seglcd send \-\-cpu\-temp 42 \-\-gpu\-temp 57 \-\-duration 20
seglcd live \-\-show \-\-fan\-sensor it8686_31050607:fan1 \-\-pump\-sensor it8686_31050607:fan5
seglcd probe \-\-offsets 36\-63 \-\-auto 3
tools/extract\-packets.sh capture.pcapng 3 | seglcd decode \-\-diff
.EE
